The points are not close to the surface, I attached some more informative images of neurons inside a 3D rendering of the standard brain (don't mind the quality of the 3D volume, this is just our current working model). the only thing I can say is that the error seem to be most prevalent in areas where there is little or none staining. We use synapsin as a counterstain which leaves out most soma and the tracts.

Our template brain includes all of the brain volume we register (actually even a bit more just to be safe). Therefore I'm not quite sure how these points can be outside of the warping registration.

